          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            a
            %em function type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            for two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            In a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
            of the type theory in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponential object
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} function set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+type"} dependent product type
          %p
            Function types are important because they allow the user to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantification"} quantify
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            functions are sets and one could quantify over sets, while in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+set+theory"} structural set theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sort"} sort
            of functions. However, in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash b(x):B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universes"} type universes
            represent types.
