                    \\mathrm{assoc}_{A, B, C, D}(f, g, h) \equiv \mathrm{idtohomotopy}_{A, D}(h \circ_{A, C, D} (g \circ_{A, B, C} f), (h \circ_{B, C, D} g) \circ_{A, B, D} f)^{-1}(\mathrm{assoch}_{A, B, C, D}(f, g, h)):\\
                    h \circ_{A, C, D} (g \circ_{A, B, C} f) =_{A \to D} (h \circ_{B, C, D} g) \circ_{A, B, D} f
                    \\end{array}
            %p
          %h3#typal_congruence_rules Typal congruence rules
          %p
            These are called
            %em typal congruence rules
            because they are the analogue of the judgmental
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence+rules"} congruence rules
            which use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+types"} equivalence types
            instead of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
          %h4#strict_function_types_2 Strict function types
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            are negative types, we first present the typal congruence rule for the elimination rule of function types
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Given types
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:A \to B
              and an identification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:f =_{A \to B} g
              there are families of identifications
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} compelim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash \mathrm{compelim}(f, g, p)(x):f(x) =_B g(x)
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              We simply define the dependent function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} compelim
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{compelim}
              to be the canonical inductively defined function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} idtohomotopy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{idtohomotopy}
              which takes identifications between functions to homotopies between functions.
          %p The next is the typal congruence rule for the introduction rule of function types. However, unlike the case for the other two rules, one needs function extensionality.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Assuming
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash b(x):B
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash b'(x):B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identifications"} identifications
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash p(x):b(x) =_B b'(x)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} congintro
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo .
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{congintro}_{x:A.p(x)}:\lambda (x:A).b(x) =_{A \to B} \lambda (x:A).b'(x)
            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p By the computation rule of strict function types, there are families of judgmental equalities
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi λ
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo .
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash ((\lambda x:A.b(x))(x) \equiv b(x):B
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi λ
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo .
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash ((\lambda x:A.b'(x))(x) \equiv b'(x):B
            %p
              Thus, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+rules"} structural rules
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi λ
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo .
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi λ
